From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:22:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu diagnostics: off by default behind JIHAD_GPU_LOG; the
 page's transactions on the timeline

T-512: the GPU path's [jihad-gpu] diagnostics print only with JIHAD_GPU_LOG=1, or in a device round's
JIHAD_GPU_TIMELINE, JIHAD_GPU_VERIFY or JIHAD_GPU_DUMP_EVERY (one gate, gfx/2d/JihadGpuLog.h, exported
as mozilla/gfx/JihadGpuLog.h); failures and fallbacks print anyway. A daemon on the GPU path now logs
three startup lines from the engine instead of hundreds.

T-517: with JIHAD_GPU_TIMELINE a layer transaction that holds the compositor thread 3 ms or more is
logged with its parts (compositable ops and their tile uploads, layers updated, end), and every compose
job with its uploads: the express lane's frames queue behind the page's transactions.
---
